WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.563
My role in the neighbourhood,
really: I'm part of the committee,

2
00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:08.566
of the association here in Penajóia.
I'm the treasurer.

3
00:00:09.056 --> 00:00:11.634
Really, we started out
with that possibility,

4
00:00:11.718 --> 00:00:16.718
to have our community fully clear,

5
00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:20.270
in the sense of helping one another.

6
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:24.797
Really, we're here for one purpose:

7
00:00:25.148 --> 00:00:28.940
to be aware that we live
in a neighbourhood...

8
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.715
Can this neighbourhood be legalised?

9
00:00:34.846 --> 00:00:36.837
Yes, we believe so.

10
00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:40.901
And our real concern right now

11
00:00:41.432 --> 00:00:47.027
is the demolition we had
the day before yesterday.

12
00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:50.250
And that caught us by surprise.

13
00:00:50.865 --> 00:00:56.262
Another thing, even more worrying,
is that essential possibility,

14
00:00:56.346 --> 00:01:02.397
which is water and electricity, which
we lack, which we want them to give us,

15
00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:05.750
for dignity, for humanity.

16
00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:12.625
And on what terms?
On terms that we can pay. We want that.

17
00:01:12.709 --> 00:01:16.520
We've been working on it
for a long time, chasing after it.

18
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.452
A post service, really,
so we can receive our letters,

19
00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:24.119
the obligations we have.

20
00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:26.880
We're working for that. We want that.

21
00:01:26.964 --> 00:01:32.416
We don't want anything for free,
like people go around saying,

22
00:01:32.786 --> 00:01:36.524
that these people are living
at the expense of the Portuguese,

23
00:01:36.608 --> 00:01:42.386
or of the neighbours over there,
who have electricity, who pay for it.

24
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:45.742
We work too, we pay social security,

25
00:01:45.893 --> 00:01:51.047
we have that dignity too, and we
want these things for ourselves too.

26
00:01:51.157 --> 00:01:52.974
We're human, we're people.

27
00:01:53.058 --> 00:01:58.012
We came from our country,
we left our home there, our family.

28
00:01:58.162 --> 00:02:02.340
It's not that we want to live in this
neighbourhood or in these conditions.

29
00:02:04.187 --> 00:02:08.166
It's because we can't
afford an affordable rent.

30
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.382
Because here in Portugal, right now,

31
00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:17.412
everyone knows the conditions
really aren't there.

32
00:02:17.496 --> 00:02:24.991
Rent above wages, below...
So we have to understand that.

33
00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:27.312
People have to understand,

34
00:02:27.703 --> 00:02:33.663
we have to give each other a hand, we have
to treat each other as humans, as beings,

35
00:02:33.747 --> 00:02:38.099
because we were really born
to be like this one day.
